  "reply_text": "Found **one merge-blocking bug**:\n\n**[P1] `topTags` mutates its input, corrupting the sidebar’s recent strip** — `src/tags.js:10`\n`tags.sort(...)` reorders the caller’s array in place. `sidebar()` then reads that same array at `src/render.js:5`, so “recent” becomes the five highest-count tags instead of the first five originally supplied. This also violates the documented non-mutation contract.\n\nReproduced: input order `a,b,c,d,e,f` yielded recent tags `b,f,c,e,d` instead of `a,b,c,d,e`.\n\n**Recommended fix:** sort a copy (`[...tags].sort(...)`). Add regression tests asserting that `topTags` leaves its input unchanged and `sidebar().recent` preserves the original order.\n\nAll four existing tests pass, but none covers this regression. No files changed.",
